  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Jeremiah",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 32,
    "summary": "Jeremiah is imprisoned by Zedekiah—The prophet purchases land to symbolize the return of Israel to their land—The Lord will gather Israel and make an everlasting covenant with them.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "The word that came to Jeremiah from the Lord in the tenth year of Zedekiah king of Judah, which was the eighteenth year of Nebuchadrezzar.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 99
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:1",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "For then the king of Babylon’s army besieged Jerusalem: and Jeremiah the prophet was shut up in the court of the prison, which was in the king of Judah’s house.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 24:20."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 127,
            "end": 130
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Kgs. 24:20.",
            "prettyString": "2 Kings 24:20",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2kings",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 24,
                    "end": 24,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 20,
                        "end": 20
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:2",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "For Zedekiah king of Judah had shut him up, saying, Wherefore dost thou prophesy, and say, Thus saith the Lord, Behold, I will give this city into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he shall take it;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:3",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And Zedekiah king of Judah shall not escape out of the hand of the Chaldeans, but shall surely be delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon, and shall speak with him mouth to mouth, and his eyes shall behold his eyes;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:4",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And he shall lead Zedekiah to Babylon, and there shall he be until I visit him, saith the Lord: though ye fight with the Chaldeans, ye shall not prosper?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "TG Israel, Bondage of, in Other Lands."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Israel, Bondage of, in Other Lands.",
            "prettyString": "TG Israel, Bondage of, in Other Lands",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Israel, Bondage of, in Other Lands",
                "entryId": "tg-israel-bondage-of-in-other-lands",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:5",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jeremiah said, The word of the Lord came unto me, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:6",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, Hanameel the son of Shallum thine uncle shall come unto thee, saying, Buy thee my field that is in Anathoth: for the right of redemption is thine to buy it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 103
          },
          {
            "start": 145,
            "end": 147
          },
          {
            "start": 161,
            "end": 164
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:7",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "So Hanameel mine uncle’s son came to me in the court of the prison according to the word of the Lord, and said unto me, Buy my field, I pray thee, that is in Anathoth, which is in the country of Benjamin: for the right of inheritance is thine, and the redemption is thine; buy it for thyself. Then I knew that this was the word of the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 152,
            "end": 154
          },
          {
            "start": 174,
            "end": 176
          },
          {
            "start": 234,
            "end": 236
          },
          {
            "start": 263,
            "end": 265
          },
          {
            "start": 277,
            "end": 279
          },
          {
            "start": 315,
            "end": 318
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:8",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And I bought the field of Hanameel my uncle’s son, that was in Anathoth, and weighed him the money, even seventeen shekels of silver.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 84,
            "text": "Gen. 23:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 59
          },
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 104
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Gen. 23:16.",
            "prettyString": "Genesis 23:16",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "genesis",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 23,
                    "end": 23,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 16,
                        "end": 16
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:9",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And I subscribed the evidence, and sealed it, and took witnesses, and weighed him the money in the balances.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 45
          },
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 81
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:10",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "So I took the evidence of the purchase, both that which was sealed according to the law and custom, and that which was open:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 44
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 76
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:11",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And I gave the evidence of the purchase unto Baruch the son of Neriah, the son of Maaseiah, in the sight of Hanameel mine uncle’s son, and in the presence of the witnesses that subscribed the book of the purchase, before all the Jews that sat in the court of the prison.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "Jer. 43:3."
          },
          {
            "start": 192,
            "end": 196,
            "text": "OR deed."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 130,
            "end": 134
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Jer. 43:3.",
            "prettyString": "Jeremiah 43:3",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "jeremiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 43,
                    "end": 43,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 3,
                        "end": 3
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:12",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And I charged Baruch before them, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:13",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Thus saith the Lord of hosts, the God of Israel; Take these evidences, this evidence of the purchase, both which is sealed, and this evidence which is open; and put them in an earthen vessel, that they may continue many days.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "OR documents."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:14",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "For thus saith the Lord of hosts, the God of Israel; Houses and fields and vineyards shall be possessed again in this land.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:15",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Now when I had delivered the evidence of the purchase unto Baruch the son of Neriah, I prayed unto the Lord, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:16",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "Ah Lord God! behold, thou hast made the heaven and the earth by thy great power and stretched out arm, and there is nothing too hard for thee:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 128,
            "end": 132,
            "text": "TG God, Power of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 106
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG God, Power of.",
            "prettyString": "TG God, Power of",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "God, Power of",
                "entryId": "tg-god-power-of",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:17",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou shewest lovingkindness unto thousands, and recompensest the iniquity of the fathers into the bosom of their children after them: the Great, the Mighty God, the Lord of hosts, is his name,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 180,
            "end": 182
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:18",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Great in counsel, and mighty in work: for thine eyes are open upon all the ways of the sons of men: to give every one according to his ways, and according to the fruit of his doings:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 107,
            "text": "TG Reward."
          },
          {
            "start": 135,
            "end": 139,
            "text": "TG Good Works; Justice."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 56
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Reward.",
            "prettyString": "TG Reward",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Reward",
                "entryId": "tg-reward",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "raw": "TG Good Works; Justice.",
            "prettyString": "TG Good Works; TG Justice",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
