            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:19",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "Which hast set signs and wonders in the land of Egypt, even unto this day, and in Israel, and among other men; and hast made thee a name, as at this day;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 59
          },
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 105
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:20",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "And hast brought forth thy people Israel out of the land of Egypt with signs, and with wonders, and with a strong hand, and with a stretched out arm, and with great terror;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:21",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "And hast given them this land, which thou didst swear to their fathers to give them, a land flowing with milk and honey;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:22",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "And they came in, and possessed it; but they obeyed not thy voice, neither walked in thy law; they have done nothing of all that thou commandedst them to do: therefore thou hast caused all this evil to come upon them:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:23",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold the mounts, they are come unto the city to take it; and the city is given into the hand of the Chaldeans, that fight against it, because of the sword, and of the famine, and of the pestilence: and what thou hast spoken is come to pass; and, behold, thou seest it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 267,
            "end": 270
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:24",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "And thou hast said unto me, O Lord God, Buy thee the field for money, and take witnesses; for the city is given into the hand of the Chaldeans.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:25",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "Then came the word of the Lord unto Jeremiah, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:26",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, I am the Lord, the God of all flesh: is there any thing too hard for me?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 12
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:27",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore thus saith the Lord; Behold, I will give this city into the hand of the Chaldeans, and into the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, and he shall take it:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:28",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "And the Chaldeans, that fight against this city, shall come and set fire on this city, and burn it with the houses, upon whose roofs they have offered incense unto Baal, and poured out drink offerings unto other gods, to provoke me to anger.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 127,
            "end": 132,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 23:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Kgs. 23:12.",
            "prettyString": "2 Kings 23:12",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2kings",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 23,
                    "end": 23,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 12,
                        "end": 12
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:29",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "For the children of Israel and the children of Judah have only done evil before me from their youth: for the children of Israel have only provoked me to anger with the work of their hands, saith the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 153,
            "end": 158,
            "text": "TG Anger."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Anger.",
            "prettyString": "TG Anger",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Anger",
                "entryId": "tg-anger",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:30",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "For this city hath been to me as a provocation of mine anger and of my fury from the day that they built it even unto this day; that I should remove it from before my face,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 32
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:31",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 31
      },
      {
        "text": "Because of all the evil of the children of Israel and of the children of Judah, which they have done to provoke me to anger, they, their kings, their princes, their priests, and their prophets, and the men of Judah, and the inhabitants of Jerusalem.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 32,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 32:32",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 32,
        "verse": 32
      },
      {
        "text": "And they have turned unto me the back, and not the face: though I taught them, rising up early and teaching them, yet they have not hearkened to receive instruction.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "Jer. 2:27; Ezek. 8:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 113
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 33,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Jer. 2:27; Ezek. 8:16.",
            "prettyString": "Jeremiah 2:27; Ezekiel 8:16",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "jeremiah",
